Vulnerable: Stores user files under webroot with original names; no checks.
Hardened: Stores outside webroot (data/storage) with randomized names; metadata in SQLite.

Vulnerable: Accepts any content type and extension.
Hardened: Extension whitelist (png, jpg/jpeg, pdf) and python-magic sniffing. Pillow verifies images; PyPDF2 validates PDFs.

Vulnerable: No size limits.
Hardened: Enforces configurable max size (default 5 MB); rejects with 413.

Vulnerable: No malware scanning.
Hardened: Scans via clamd (pyclamd) if available; infected files quarantined (returns 451). Gracefully handles missing ClamAV.

Vulnerable: Direct static serving; no auth.
Hardened: Signed temporary tokens (HMAC-SHA256) required for downloads; secure headers.

Vulnerable: No rate limiting or structured logging.
Hardened: Per-IP rate limiting; structured logging; explicit JSON error handling.
